      "groups": [
        {
          "id": "R1",
          "title": "Every controlling plan input serializes with Apply",
          "note": "One per-person transaction-scoped constraint lock taken first by approval, rebase and Apply and by every canonical writer of calendar mirrors, reservations, profile, time off, blocks and Today; database triggers make any other writer participate, so new meetings and reservations cannot appear unserialized. A writer that commits first makes Apply refuse until rebase; one that starts during Apply waits for it.",
          "evidence": [
            {
